In particular people need to do the following

```
@QuarkusTest
public class MyTests
@Test
	public void testThatAPersonCanBeRetrievedByName() {
		
		/callInTransaction();
		
		// When
		final Person retByID = Person.findById(person.id);
		final Person retByName = Person.findByName("Bob");
		
		// Then
		Assertions.assertNotNull(retByID);
		Assertions.assertNotNull(retByName);
	}

        @Transactional // note the private, should we make things public by bytecode transformation? or throw an exception
        private void callInTransaction() {
		// Given
		final Person person = new Person();
		person.name = "Bob";
		person.birth = LocalDate.now();
		person.status = Status.ALIVE;
		
		person.persist();

        }
}
```

@mkouba because I would have done it like that not knowing the CDI restrictions. Since it's build time bytecode enhancement, you could make the self invocation intercept ;)
But we would go far from the spec which probably sucks unless we restrict it to tests maybe?

Or simply have a `doInTransaction` helper method that would do the tx start / stop for the user @Sanne ?
